WEBVTT

00:00:01.610 --> 00:00:04.780
The festival of dreams
to crown the strongest Pokémon Trainer...

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:08.320
The Pokémon World Championships
Masters Tournament.

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:12.910
At long last, Dande and Satoshi’s
finals battle has begun.

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:19.750
A fierce fight right out of the gate,
with Dande losing Inteleon and Satoshi losing Gänger.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.670
They both have five Pokémon left.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:25.420
Their battle continues to heat up!

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:36.680
Psycho Field on top of
the frozen ground, huh...?

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:41.060
Come on, Satoshi!
What Pokémon will you use next?

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:44.980
Negigaknight! I choose you!

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:55.030
A Fighting type?

00:00:55.580 --> 00:01:00.920
Barrikohru is part Psychic type,
so the Fighting-type Negigaknight is at a disadvantage.

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:07.920
Satoshi! Negigaknight!
Go for it!

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:11.800
Negigaknight!
There’s something only you can do!

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:13.260
I’m counting on you!

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:55.860
Consecutive Cut!

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:10.210
A ferocious assault from Negigaknight!
But Barrikohru also wields its staff masterfully!

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:11.840
Go, go, go!

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:13.550
Send it flying with that big leek!

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:16.300
Avenge Gänger, meow!

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:32.570
Consecutive Cut hits!
It’s super effective against Psychic types!

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:34.150
Brutal Swing!

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:39.870
Barrikohru! Catch it!

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:48.250
Wide Force!

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:02.350
This time, Negigaknight takes
a super effective hit!

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:11.270
Psycho Field and Wide Force
make for a terrifying combination!

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:13.730
You okay, Negigaknight?!

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:19.030
Good job holding out.

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:23.030
He has Negigaknight’s
chivalrous spirit to thank for that.

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:26.790
Triple Axel!

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:43.970
Wide Force!

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:47.810
Detect!

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:56.480
Go get your shield!

00:04:57.240 --> 00:04:59.280
And he leaps!

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:02.320
Whoa!

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:05.160
A pole vault?

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:06.870
Then we’ll use...

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:08.120
Triple Axel!

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:18.130
Let’s make this work!

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:19.760
Consecutive Cut!

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:21.340
Here he comes, Barrikohru!

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:23.220
Cut...

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:24.140
...the field!

00:05:34.150 --> 00:05:36.940
The Psycho Field energy...

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:39.440
...has vanished!

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:41.700
Great job, Negigaknight!

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:45.870
So that was your goal!

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:50.710
Because it was a Bug-type move,
it could destroy the Psychic-type move?

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:54.170
So moves aren’t <i>just</i>
for attacking Pokémon...

00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:56.710
Right! This is how Satoshi battles.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:58.710
Negigaknight, return!

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:02.880
I’ll finish this with you.

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:12.890
Watch out.
There’s no telling what he’s planning.

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:16.480
Let’s do it, Lucario!

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:23.110
The bond between us...

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:27.200
Mega Evolve!

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:51.520
Competitor Satoshi follows his Kyodaimax
with Mega Evolution!

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:00.440
Aura!

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:01.900
I’m really feeling it!

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:03.400
Wow...

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:07.030
You can feel Lucario’s determination!

00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:12.040
Incredible Aura from Lucario!

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:17.250
Bullet Punch!

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:18.580
Triple Axel!

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:26.050
It dodged!

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:31.140
Even without Psycho Field,
the frozen field still gives Barrikohru the advantage!

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:35.980
Triple Axel hits!

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:37.270
Lucario!

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:41.730
Barrikohru!
Another Triple Axel!

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:51.830
Still going, huh?

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:54.200
Can’t underestimate Mega Evolution.

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:59.130
Lucario! Use your Aura!

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:05.210
Sense Barrikohru’s movements!

00:08:13.890 --> 00:08:15.100
Hmm?

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:20.600
Charge up an Aura Sphere!

00:08:24.110 --> 00:08:28.450
Very well!
Just <i>try</i> and follow Barrikohru with your Aura!

00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:29.610
Triple Axel!

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:51.260
Now! Fire!

00:08:55.220 --> 00:09:00.640
Mega Lucario counters!
It really could sense Barrikohru’s movements!

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:03.520
Barrikohru is unable to battle!

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:06.400
We did it, Lucario!

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:14.990
Competitor Dande
loses a second Pokémon.

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:18.290
A stellar performance, Barrikohru!
Return!

00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:23.210
You’re quite something,
Satoshi, Lucario.

00:09:23.210 --> 00:09:26.340
Well, that’s because
I believe in Lucario!

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:31.220
This one’s next!

00:09:31.220 --> 00:09:33.090
Come out! Drapult!

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:37.600
Lucario! Shadow Clones!

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:44.610
Follow up with Bullet Punch!

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:53.570
Flamethrower!

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:02.790
Return, Lucario.

00:10:04.210 --> 00:10:06.670
You’re up next, Uonoragon!

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:16.180
Ooh, it’s turned into a showdown
between Dragon types!

00:10:16.180 --> 00:10:17.640
Dragon Dive!

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:24.940
Dragon Arrow!

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:29.400
Catch it!

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:36.450
The second
Dragon Arrow missile fails!

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:39.030
What?

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:44.540
I’ll take that back.
One more Dragon Arrow!

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:55.720
You okay, Uonoragon?!

00:11:03.730 --> 00:11:06.730
What is happening
to Uonoragon?!

00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:47.520
You okay, Uonoragon?!

00:11:55.530 --> 00:11:58.450
What is happening
to Uonoragon?!

00:12:15.010 --> 00:12:16.340
Uonoragon...

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:20.930
Uonoragon’s body is changing?!
What is going on?!

00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:23.850
Forget it!
Let’s do this, Drapult!

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:32.360
The clash of Dragon moves must’ve awakened
some long-dormant power within Uonoragon.

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:36.690
I wonder how Satoshi
will make use of this metamorphosis.

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:38.070
100,000 Volts!

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:45.870
You didn’t get to
let it shine after all.

00:12:45.870 --> 00:12:47.410
Finish it! Move in!

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:51.040
Uonoragon!

00:12:58.590 --> 00:12:59.340
What?!

00:12:59.970 --> 00:13:00.720
Okay!

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:03.600
What are those spikes?!

00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:05.760
All right! It caught it!

00:13:06.350 --> 00:13:08.770
Now, Uonoragon! Jaw Bite!

00:13:12.690 --> 00:13:14.440
It bit on!

00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:18.440
Uonoragon counters!
Drapult can’t get away!

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:24.700
What power...

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:27.410
It squeezes even tighter!

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:31.580
This is like Otosupus’s Octolock.

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:36.960
But, Satoshi, you shouldn’t
underestimate Drapult.

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:39.300
Dragon Tail!

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:45.680
Incredible!
Drapult’s tail stretched out!

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:49.060
Don’t let go! Ice Fang!

00:14:02.280 --> 00:14:03.950
Kairyu!

00:14:03.950 --> 00:14:09.330
There it goes! Sending a Pokémon flying
and forcing a swap to a reserve Pokémon!

00:14:09.330 --> 00:14:12.040
That’s the effect of Dragon Tail!

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:13.500
Can that happen?!

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:16.500
And <i>right</i> when Uonoragon
had awakened, too!

00:14:16.880 --> 00:14:18.670
Good going, Big Bro!

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:22.130
Drapult!
You’re facing another Dragon type!

00:14:22.760 --> 00:14:24.640
Dragon Arrow!

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:29.140
Fly, Kairyu! Dragon Dance!

00:14:33.020 --> 00:14:36.020
Kairyu speeds up with Dragon Dance!

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:41.490
But the Dragon Arrows
are locked on to their target!

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:46.030
Dragon Claw!

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:06.680
After them, Kairyu!

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:11.770
Dragon Tail!

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:23.280
Dragon Tail again!

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:26.860
This time,
it dragged out Mega Lucario!

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:30.830
Satoshi must be finding this hard.

00:15:30.830 --> 00:15:33.790
Satoshi may have scored more wins,

00:15:33.790 --> 00:15:36.670
but Competitor Dande’s
still setting the pace.

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:41.750
Don’t worry, Pikachu.

00:15:51.510 --> 00:15:54.060
Lucario!
I’ll finish this with you!

00:15:55.770 --> 00:15:56.810
Bullet Punch!

00:15:59.440 --> 00:16:01.610
A swift assault from Lucario!

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:06.030
100,000 Volts!

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:08.410
Reversal!

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:20.170
Bullet Punch!

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:25.300
Lucario?!

00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:29.180
Oh! Mega Lucario was paralysed!

00:16:32.930 --> 00:16:34.180
Flamethrower!

00:16:52.870 --> 00:16:55.080
Lucario is unable to battle!

00:16:55.540 --> 00:17:00.080
Competitor Dande’s second win!
It’s a 4v4 now!

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:02.500
Good work, Drapult!

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:04.920
Return, Lucario.

00:17:08.760 --> 00:17:10.380
You did well out there.

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:14.850
Mr. Dande really is strong...

00:17:14.850 --> 00:17:17.350
He’s quick to close any gap...

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:22.980
Dande’s smile
shows he’s not worried.

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:24.310
Satoshi...

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:26.980
It’ll be fine.
He’s going to be fine.

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:28.690
That Drapult’s unbelievable!

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:31.030
Is the brat boy gonna be okay...?

00:17:31.030 --> 00:17:35.580
Pull yourself together!
We’re here watching you!

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:41.500
What’s wrong, Satoshi?
My Drapult is still raring to go!

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:47.130
Competitor Dande taunts
Competitor Satoshi!

00:17:47.130 --> 00:17:50.130
How will Competitor Satoshi
respond?

00:17:52.970 --> 00:17:54.550
Kairyu! I choose you!

00:17:59.810 --> 00:18:03.730
This time,
Competitor Satoshi sends out Kairyu.

00:18:03.730 --> 00:18:05.860
Let’s go! Hurricane!

00:18:10.820 --> 00:18:14.990
An intense Hurricane
buffets Drapult!

00:18:15.410 --> 00:18:16.990
All right! It’s working!

00:18:21.250 --> 00:18:23.370
Use a massive 100,000 Volts!

00:18:38.850 --> 00:18:41.520
The 100,000 Volts
destroyed the Hurricane?!

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:48.020
What do you think?
It was simple!

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:51.230
Then...
Fly up high, Kairyu!

00:18:53.570 --> 00:18:54.700
Dragon Arrow!

00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:57.990
Draco Meteor!

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:08.090
Drapult, dodge them all!

00:19:15.760 --> 00:19:20.970
The Dragon Arrows are shot down!
But Drapult closes in on Kairyu!

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:23.480
Kairyu, grab Drapult!

00:19:25.980 --> 00:19:27.480
100,000 Volts!

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:37.740
Let’s go! Dra-Kairyu Meteor!

00:19:38.120 --> 00:19:39.660
Dra-Kairyu Meteor?!

00:19:40.910 --> 00:19:42.620
She made herself the meteor?!

00:19:42.620 --> 00:19:45.120
Go, go!

00:20:07.190 --> 00:20:09.650
Drapult is unable to battle!

00:20:12.150 --> 00:20:15.190
Competitor Satoshi
struggled against Dragon Tail,

00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:18.160
but he managed to pull out
a third win!

00:20:18.160 --> 00:20:20.320
Now <i>that</i> shocked everyone!

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:23.660
His finishing blow was the
Dra-Kairyu Meteor he invented right here!

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:31.460
Thank you, Kairyu!

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:34.760
Return, Drapult!

00:20:36.590 --> 00:20:38.180
You were really cool out there.

00:20:40.930 --> 00:20:44.060
Satoshi... You really are the best!

00:20:45.520 --> 00:20:48.480
But have you noticed?

00:20:48.480 --> 00:20:53.860
All your remaining Pokémon
are already worn out.

00:21:07.540 --> 00:21:09.160
Come out, Gorillander!

00:21:34.190 --> 00:21:36.900
A true seesaw struggle.

00:21:37.780 --> 00:21:40.240
Satoshi faces Monarch Dande.

00:21:40.240 --> 00:21:41.990
Their fierce fight
continues!

00:23:06.320 --> 00:23:10.870
<i>Pokémon World Championships
Masters Tournament News!</i>

00:23:11.620 --> 00:23:13.870
The back-and-forth continues
in the finals battle!

00:23:13.870 --> 00:23:16.040
His Kyodaimax is finally here!

00:23:16.040 --> 00:23:19.170
The sublime power of Kyodai Hellfire
engulfs the field!

00:23:19.170 --> 00:23:21.210
Competitor Satoshi
starts feeling cornered!

00:23:21.210 --> 00:23:23.920
Don’t worry!
Pikachu’ll work something out!

00:23:23.920 --> 00:23:26.300
Go get him!
That’s our Pikachu!

00:23:26.300 --> 00:23:27.510
That’s right!

00:23:27.510 --> 00:23:29.430
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:29.430 --> 00:23:31.140
The Finals Three - “Supreme”

00:23:31.140 --> 00:23:33.730
Correction: “The Finals III,” meow.
